Fix the panel digest so it can actually answer "did the GUI take the screen?".

Two bugs, both invisible in the previous images:

1. m= was always 0.
   0109 added `m=%d` to the report and passed sweet_console_muted -- but
   panel_report() clears that flag on its very first line, so the value it
   printed was the one it had just written, never the state of the world.
   The flag now is captured before it is touched, and a new gui= field
   reports panel_yielded directly.

2. After the GUI took the screen, the phone went silent.
   0109 reported once, set panel_yielded and then stopped reporting for
   good (`else if (panel_fbswaps == 0)`).  A crash after the home screen
   appeared therefore left a frozen picture with no diagnostics at all --
   exactly the "the screen stopped moving" symptom this series was written
   to chase.  The digest is now printed every 20 s whether or not the GUI
   has taken over.  It is drawn as its own block and the console is muted
   again right after, so it does not sit on top of the home screen.

The report line is now:

    === SWEET t=<s> exec=<n> crash=<n> sb=<n>/<n> fb=<n> sw=<n> dn=<n> m=<0|1> gui=<0|1> ===

  sw=   frames that really reached the panel (0110 fixed the detector)
  m=    the console mute state before this report drew itself
  gui=  1 once a real frame was seen and the console yielded to the GUI

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -1128,10 +1128,18 @@
 static void
 panel_report(unsigned secs)
 {
+	/*
+	 * Report the mute state we are about to override, not the one we set
+	 * below: 0109 printed sweet_console_muted right after clearing it, so
+	 * m= was always 0 and could never say whether the GUI had taken the
+	 * screen.  gui= says it directly.
+	 */
+	int muted = sweet_console_muted;
+
 	sweet_console_muted = 0;                /* only our own block is drawn */
-	printf("\n\n=== SWEET t=%us exec=%u crash=%u sb=%u/%u fb=%u sw=%u dn=%u m=%d ===\n",
+	printf("\n\n=== SWEET t=%us exec=%u crash=%u sb=%u/%u fb=%u sw=%u dn=%u m=%d gui=%d ===\n",
 	    secs, panel_execs, panel_crashes, panel_sbexec, panel_sbcrash,
-	    panel_fbseen, panel_fbswaps, panel_denied, sweet_console_muted);
+	    panel_fbseen, panel_fbswaps, panel_denied, muted, panel_yielded);
 	panel_dump(panel_fb, PANEL_FB, panel_fb_at, "-- fb --");
 	panel_dump(panel_sb, PANEL_SB, panel_sb_at, "-- springboard --");
 	if (panel_top_used != 0) {
@@ -1175,7 +1183,17 @@
 				panel_report(secs);
 				panel_yielded = TRUE;
 				sweet_console_muted = 1;
-			} else if (panel_fbswaps == 0) {
+			} else {
+				/*
+				 * Keep reporting after the yield as well.  0109
+				 * stopped reporting entirely once the GUI had
+				 * taken the screen, so a later crash left a frozen
+				 * picture with no diagnostics at all -- exactly the
+				 * "the screen stopped moving" symptom.  The report
+				 * is drawn as its own block and the console is
+				 * muted again right after, so it does not sit on
+				 * top of the GUI.
+				 */
 				panel_report(secs);
 			}
 			/* the report is in the ring now: never ingest our own text */
 			scan = sweet_log_position();
 			panel_used = 0;
